    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive outlook for the Austin Waves centers on capitalizing against the weak arm of Gibson. **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier play with a 76.03 score; while he faces an elite-hold pitcher in Soriano, his elite sprint speed and favorable platoon dynamics offer our highest ceiling for stolen bases. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** follows closely at 71.10, benefiting from a robust BvP history and a strong platoon split against Nola. Despite hitting in the 8-hole, **Josh Lowe** remains a core start (70.08) because he exploits the same vulnerable Gibson matchup as **Nolan Schanuel** (69.69) and **Wade Meckler** (59.97). By stacking these assets against Gibson, we are aggressively chasing R and RBI upside in what is statistically our most favorable pitching environment of the day.\n\nDeciding the final bench spots required nuance, with **Jacob Wilson** (56.37) narrowly missing the cut. While **Jacob Wilson** shows consistent floor potential, the optimizer prioritized the specific platoon advantages of **Cole Carrigg** (60.28) and **Wade Meckler** against their respective matchups. **Miguel Vargas** and **Josh Jung** were also considered but remain relegated to the bench, as their lack of elite speed\u2014our primary scarcity target\u2014renders them less efficient than the high-upside speed profiles currently locked into our starting OF. While we are confident in this lineup, monitor potential weather flags; our heavy reliance on the Gibson matchup means any rain delays in that park could disproportionately impact our daily scoring output.",
